{#
  THE TILE. One bounded, saturated, small, rare object — see components/tile.css.

  Usage:
    {% include 'partials/tile.twig' with {
         meaning: 'award-decided', label: 'Overall winner · won twice'
       } only %}

  `meaning`, never a role name and never a hue: Accent::for() throws on a meaning
  nobody defined, so a typo stops the build rather than rendering the wrong state.
  A page that says "withheld" in caution red when it meant "form error" is worse
  than a page that fails.

  The MARK is aria-hidden and the LABEL is not. The colour is an accelerator on a
  word, never the fact itself — which is the rule that keeps the palette honest
  for the ~1 in 12 men with a colour vision deficiency, and for every screen
  reader.
#}
<span class="ag-tile{{ size|default('') == 'lg' ? ' ag-tile--lg' : '' }}{{ live|default(false) ? ' ag-tile--live' : '' }}"
      style="{{ tile_style(meaning) }}">
  <span class="ag-tile__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span>{{ label }}</span>
</span>
